
دوائي المنزلي — Multi-Side Medicine Box Scan
Implementation prompt for a coding agent (offline OCR only; no barcode/GTIN scanning)
Use this prompt with the existing Flutter project, especially add_medicine_screen.dart, dosage_gate.dart, expiry_service.dart, the MedicineDraft/MedForm definitions, app navigation, localization files, and the current database/repository layer.

1. Role and objective
Act as a senior Flutter engineer working inside an existing production-style Flutter app named دوائي المنزلي. Implement a feature called “مسح علبة الدواء” / “Scan medicine box”.

The user takes 1–6 photos of different sides of a medicine package (front, back, side panels, and optional flap). The app recognizes printed text locally on the device, combines evidence from all photos, and presents a review screen. After review, the feature passes a MedicineDraft to the existing AddMedicineScreen(prefill: draft) flow. The user must review the prefilled data in the existing form and explicitly save it there.

This is an implementation task, not a request for a plan or a standalone demo. Inspect the existing app, implement the feature in its conventions, add tests, run the available checks, and report exactly what passed and what remains blocked.

Priority order
Medical and data safety.
Compatibility with the existing app and its models.
Genuine on-device/offline processing and privacy.
Correct field extraction and conflict handling.
Usable Arabic RTL and English UI.
Convenience and performance.
