3. Non-negotiable safety and scope rules
OCR only — absolutely no barcode processing
Do not use GTIN, GS1 Application Identifiers, GS1 DataMatrix, barcode decoding, or product-code lookup in this feature.
Do not call mobile_scanner, BarcodeScanService, or any existing barcode workflow from the box-scan flow.
Do not add a GS1 parser.
MedicineDraft.barcode must remain empty/null according to the existing model contract. The separate existing barcode feature remains separate.
Ignore barcode stripes, DataMatrix squares, registration numbers, phone numbers, and long digit strings. Never interpret an unlabelled number string near a barcode as a batch number or date.
Only permitted fields
OCR may propose values only for fields represented by the existing project model that correspond to:

Trade/brand name.
Active ingredient text.
Strength (for example, 500 mg, 250 mg/5 mL, or 1%).
Dosage form, using only valid values from the existing MedForm enum.
Manufacturer.
Batch/lot number.
Expiry date.
Manufacturing/production date.
Pack quantity/size.
A storage-condition hint; if the existing model uses needsRefrigeration, it may propose a value only as described below and it must require explicit user confirmation.
Never fill dosage, directions, indications, warnings, contraindications, interactions, or any other medical advice field from OCR. Such information must continue to come only from the app's verified SourceReference/DosageGate flow. If MedicineDraft requires these properties, use the existing safe empty/default behavior; do not populate them from package text.

Human review is mandatory
OCR creates a draft only. It must never save a medicine or write to the database.
Every proposed field must be shown as machine-extracted and needing review until the user edits or explicitly confirms it. Use the existing form's supported review/dirty state if available; otherwise add a small, explicit confirmation state without breaking manual entry.
Expiry date always requires a deliberate confirmation tap, even when confidence is high.
Low-confidence or ambiguous fields remain empty and show candidate alternatives where useful. Never guess to make the form look complete.
If the parsed expiry date is in the past, show the existing expired warning using SafetyStrings.expiredDisposal in the review flow. Do not bypass or duplicate the app's established expiry-safety logic.
The user must still be able to edit or remove every proposed value before saving in AddMedicineScreen.
Offline processing and privacy
All image processing, OCR, parsing, and merging must run on-device. Do not upload images or extracted text, call cloud OCR/LLM APIs, or add network requests for recognition.
Verify the chosen engine/model configuration supports the intended offline behavior. If an engine might fetch its model at first run, do not claim the feature is fully offline until its supported bundled/offline configuration has been verified. Prefer a bundled model or a fully local fallback.
Camera permission must be requested only when the user opens this feature and needs the camera.
Clean up temporary images after cancellation and after the scan session finishes, except for an image explicitly retained through an existing, supported package-photo feature. Do not invent persistent photo storage if the app has no such feature.
Do not add analytics, logging, or crash reports containing package images, recognized text, batch numbers, or dates.
